## 3. First Contact: Build One Simple Page

You might still be thinking:

> “That’s nice but I still don’t know what to actually do.”

This section walks you through **one full pass**:

- build a layout  
- add text  
- add background  
- add one sticker  
- color it  
- age it  
- add one tiny motion  
- save  


### 3.1 Start with a blank board

Open the app.

If there is old content, either:

- use **New Board** / **New Project**, or  
- select old pieces and delete them.

You want an empty middle.

### 3.2 Carve basic zones

Goal:

- a header at the top  
- a main body under it  

#### Header

1. Open **Big Boxes** bin.  
2. Drag **Header Bar** onto the top of the board.  
3. Drop it.  

You should see a long strip at the top.

#### Body

1. Still in **Big Boxes**, drag **Big Box**.  
2. Drop it under the header, stretching it to fill the rest.  

Now you have two big zones:

- top strip: header  
- big box: body  

This is enough to start.

### 3.3 Put words in place

Open **Words** bin.

#### Header text

1. Drag **Big Title Words** into the header.  
2. Type something like:

   > ARRIVAL RAILS – SOUTH YARD  

You can rename later. For now it gives shape.

#### Body text

1. Drag **Normal Reading Words** into the big box.  
2. Type something like:

   > This board shows sound loads arriving on the rails.  
   > Each row is a car.  
   > Each car carries a pattern.

You now have a crude information layout:

- what this screen is  
- what it does  

### 3.4 Drop a background

Open **Backgrounds** bin.

1. Drag **Concrete Floor** into the board.  
2. Drop it anywhere.

The background behind everything should turn into a “concrete” look.

Check the **Stack Of Things**:

- `Concrete Floor` will be near the bottom.  
- The header and big box should sit on top of it.

If concrete is covering everything, drag its layer down to the very bottom.

### 3.5 Add one sticker

Open **Stickers** bin.

1. Drag **Warning Sign** near the header text.  
2. Drop it.  

Use the right panel:

- **Size & Spot**:
  - Move Left / Right  
  - Move Up / Down  
  - Make It Wider / Taller  

Place it so it feels like a hazard badge in the header.

### 3.6 Color the pieces

Switch to **Paint The Colors**, or just use **Look & Color**.

#### Header bar

1. Click the header bar.  
2. Look & Color:
   - Fill Color: deep, dark gray.  
   - Words Color (for header text): near-white or light grey.

#### Big box (body)

1. Click the big box.  
2. Look & Color:
   - Fill Color: a little lighter than header.  
   - Words Color: dark text on light or light text on dark, but high contrast.

#### Warning sign

1. Click the warning sign.  
2. Look & Color:
   - Fill Color: hazard yellow or faded yellow.  
   - Border Color: darker, maybe almost black.  
   - Words Color (if text exists): dark enough to read.

Now everything has a simple hierarchy:

- header: dark, strong  
- body: lighter, readable  
- warning: bright accent  

### 3.7 Age the page

Open **Add Dirt And Scratches**, or use dirt controls in **Look & Color**.

For the background layers:

- `Concrete Floor`:
  - Add Dirt: medium.  
  - Sharp Or Blurry: soft on the edges, sharper in the center.

For the big box and header:

- Add Dirt: small, so text stays readable.  
- Sharp Or Blurry: mostly sharp.

You want the **world** to feel old and used, but the **information** to stay legible.

### 3.8 Add one tiny motion

Choose one piece to move a little.

Good candidates:

- the warning sign  
- a small indicator icon  

For example, the warning sign.

1. Select it.  
2. Open **Move By Itself** drawer or **How Things Move** panel.  
3. Set:
   - Motion Preset: `Soft Bounce`.  
   - How Much: very low.  
   - How Fast: slow.  
   - Repeat: on.  

Click **Test Move** if you have that.

Result:

- the warning sign breathes a little, like a machine indicator  
- everything else stays still  

### 3.9 Save

Open the **Save And Take Out** panel.

Click **Save Project**.

Name it something like:

> arrival-rails-v0

You have now:

- carved zones  
- added text  
- applied background and colors  
- added one sticker  
- added dirt  
- added one subtle motion  
- saved a project  

That is a full cycle.


