## 8. Exporting And The Windows App, In Simple Terms

Last section covers getting things **out** of the builder.

You have two main paths:

- exporting work (pages, images, settings)  
- packaging the builder (Windows app)  

---

### 8.1 Exporting work

Inside the builder:

- **Save Project**  
- **Get Web Page Files**  
- **Get Picture Of This**  
- **Get Settings Only**

#### Save Project

Keeps everything:

- layout  
- theme  
- positions  

Use it when you want to come back and keep tuning.

#### Get Web Page Files

Exports HTML/CSS (and maybe JS) that you can:

- host as a page  
- hand to a developer  
- plug into a bigger app  

Use when you want your design to live outside the builder.

#### Get Picture Of This

Flattens the current view into a PNG.

Use for:

- documentation  
- static mockups  
- sharing previews  

#### Get Settings Only

Exports your theme settings as JSON:

- color tokens  
- spacing  
- fonts  
- motion defaults  
- dirt and depth settings  

Use when:

- you want to reuse the same theme on other projects  
- you want a backup of your visual rules  

---

### 8.2 The Windows app

On top of all that, you set up:

- Electron shell  
- `electron-main.js`  
- `make-installer.bat`  

The idea is simple:

- run `make-installer.bat` to create a Windows installer.  
- install the builder as a desktop app.

This does **not** export a particular page.  
It packages the **tool** itself.

So you can:

- work on one machine in dev mode,  
- ship the tool to another box as a normal user app,  
- open your saved projects or import theme settings there.

Your repo stays text-only for code and config, with binary installers ignored in `dist/`.

